\paragraph{Aspect 14: parameters bind from arguments, not names.}
The critical aspect is that parameters are bound from the arguments at
the call, not from global variables that happen to share their names
--- a misconception we observed in our own teaching.
The computed-result distractor encodes it; the zero distractor encodes
assuming parameters default to zero.

