\paragraph{Aspect 16: a list argument is shared, not copied.}
The critical aspect is that a list argument is a reference to the same
list, so a mutation inside the function is visible outside; the
unchanged-list distractor encodes the copy misconception we observed.
The aspect connects to the mutable-default example in \cref{debugging}.

