\paragraph{Aspect 32: repetition re-applies, selection applies once.}
The critical aspect is that a \mintinline{python}{while} re-applies
its body for as long as the condition holds, where an
\mintinline{python}{if} applies it once --- the \emph{repetition where
selection is needed} antipattern causing wrong results
\autocite{Bosse2021Antipatterns}.
The applied-once distractor encodes reading the loop as a selection.

