\paragraph{Aspect 51: a class is a template, not a container.}
The critical aspect is that a class is a template from which
independent objects are made --- not a container that holds its
instances, and not a database \autocite{Holland1997,Ragonis2005OOP}.
The container distractor encodes the class-holds-its-objects
misconception; form B asks the same of a built-in type, per the
catalogue's generalisation.

